## AUDIT AREA 2 — STATE MANAGEMENT

### 2.1 Current State Architecture: `useState` Everything

Every component independently manages:
- User identity (`supabase.auth.getUser()`)
- User profile (`supabase.from('profiles').select(...)`)
- Loading states
- Data arrays
- Search/filter states
- Modal open/close states

### 2.2 Critical State Issues

| # | Issue | Severity | Impact |
|---|-------|----------|--------|
| FE-09 | **Profile fetched on EVERY page mount** — Each page calls `supabase.auth.getUser()` + `profiles.select(*)`. For 5 page navigations, that's 10 redundant network calls | **Critical** | Wasted bandwidth, loading jank, race conditions |
| FE-10 | **Global mutable variables bypass React** — [DashboardLayout.tsx L13-18](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/components/layout/DashboardLayout.tsx#L13): `let globalProfile: any = null` is module-scope, mutated freely. React has no way to know when this changes | **Critical** | UI does not re-render when globals change |
| FE-11 | **Badge counts re-fetched on every realtime event** — [DashboardLayout.tsx L231-234](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/components/layout/DashboardLayout.tsx#L231): Global channel fires `fetchBadgeCounts()` on ANY change to complaints, tasks, leaves, or notifications. Each call makes 2-5 Supabase queries | **High** | At scale: any task update across the org triggers 5 badge queries for every active user |
| FE-12 | **Derived state stored as primary state** — Multiple components compute values client-side and store them in `useState` instead of deriving them inline from source data | **Medium** |
| FE-13 | **No stale-while-revalidate pattern** — Every navigation triggers fresh fetches with loading spinners. No cached data is ever shown | **High** |

### 2.3 Recommended State Architecture

| Concern | Tool | Justification |
|---------|------|---------------|
| **Server state** (DB data) | **React Query (`@tanstack/react-query`)** | Already in `package.json` (v5.83) but **never imported or used anywhere**. Provides caching, deduplication, background refresh, pagination, optimistic updates |
| **Auth/user state** | **Zustand** (lightweight global store) | Single source of truth for user profile, role, permissions. Avoids prop drilling and Context re-render issues |
| **Clock-in state** | **Zustand** | Replace module-level `globalClockedIn`, `globalLogId`, etc. |
| **UI state** (sidebar, modals) | **Local `useState`** | UI state stays component-local — this is correct |
| **Form state** | **React Hook Form** (already in deps) | Already installed but underutilized. Replace manual `useState` per field |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **React Query is already installed** (`@tanstack/react-query v5.83`) in `package.json` but is **never used** in any file. This is the single highest-impact improvement — wrapping all Supabase queries in `useQuery()` eliminates duplicate fetching, adds caching, and enables pagination with almost zero refactoring.

