## AUDIT AREA 6 — REALTIME ARCHITECTURE

### 6.1 Current Subscription Inventory

| Component | Channel Name | Table Watched | Event |
|-----------|-------------|---------------|-------|
| DashboardLayout | `global-changes` | `complaints`, `tasks`, `leaves`, `notifications` | `*` |
| FloatingChatbot | `emo-omniscient-feed` | **ALL tables** (`schema: 'public'`) | `*` |
| CandidateMessages (HR) | `hr-broadcast-ann`, `hr-broadcast-jobs`, per-candidate chat | 3 tables | `*` |
| Careers (Candidate) | `candidate-ann-feed`, `candidate-job-feed` | 2 tables | `*` |
| CandidateInterviews | Per-user dynamic channel | `interview_sessions` | `UPDATE` |

### 6.2 Critical Realtime Issues

| # | Issue | Severity |
|---|-------|----------|
| FE-16 | **FloatingChatbot subscribes to ALL database changes** — [FloatingChatbot.tsx L71-75](file:///c:/Users/veere/Downloads/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/Task-Flow-Tracker-hackathon/flowtracker/src/components/FloatingChatbot.tsx#L71): `supabase.channel('emo-omniscient-feed').on('postgres_changes', { event: '*', schema: 'public' }, ...)`. Every INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on any table in the entire database triggers this handler for every logged-in user | **Critical** |
| FE-17 | **Badge count queries fire on EVERY realtime event** — A single task update across the entire org triggers badge re-counting (4-5 queries) for every active user | **Critical** |
| FE-18 | **No channel deduplication** — If DashboardLayout + FloatingChatbot both listen to the same table, two independent channels and two independent handlers fire | **High** |
| FE-19 | **Channels not properly cleaned up on hot module reload** — Vite HMR remounts components without proper cleanup, accumulating orphaned subscriptions | **Medium** |
| FE-20 | **No debouncing on realtime handlers** — A bulk data import of 100 records fires 100 separate handler executions, each triggering full data refetches | **High** |

### 6.3 Recommended Realtime Architecture

```typescript
// Single shared channel manager
const realtimeManager = {
  subscribe(table: string, event: string, callback: Function) { ... },
  unsubscribe(id: string) { ... }
};

// Usage: debounced, deduplicated, role-filtered
useRealtimeSubscription('tasks', 'INSERT', { 
  filter: `assigned_to=eq.${userId}`,
  debounceMs: 500
});
```

