## AUDIT AREA 8 — SEARCH ARCHITECTURE

### 8.1 Current Search Implementations

| Component | Search Method | Complexity |
|-----------|-------------|------------|
| OnboardingCenter | `candidates.filter(c => c.name.includes(q) \|\| c.email.includes(q))` | **O(n) client-side scan** on every keystroke |
| CandidatePipeline | `filteredApps = applications.filter(...)` inline | **O(n)** |
| ApplicationHub | Client-side search after loading all data | **O(n)** |
| Employee WorkLogs | `filteredMyReports.filter(r => r.notes?.toLowerCase().includes(search))` | **O(n)** |

### 8.2 Issues

| # | Issue | Severity |
|---|-------|----------|
| FE-21 | **All search is client-side** — Entire dataset must be loaded before searching is possible | **High** |
| FE-22 | **No debouncing** — Filter runs on every keystroke. With 5000 records, this causes visible lag | **High** |
| FE-23 | **No indexing** — No hash maps or trie structures for O(1) lookups | **Medium** |

### 8.3 Recommendations

1. **Server-side search** for datasets >100 rows — push search query to PostgreSQL
2. **Debounce** all search inputs (300ms) using `useDeferredValue` or custom debounce hook
3. **Build lookup maps** for in-memory datasets: `Map<id, entity>` instead of repeated `.find()` calls

